    "qualityRules": [
      "Brand identity is the intentional set of verbal and visual assets—name, logo, colors, type, voice—that encode what the brand stands for.",
      "Brand positioning articulates the target, frame of reference, point of difference, and reason to believe that define competitive place.",
      "Brand awareness is the extent to which audiences recognize and recall a brand, built through distinctive assets and repeated distinctive exposures.",
      "Brand trust is the audience belief that the brand will deliver as promised—built via proof, consistency, transparency, and social evidence.",
      "Brand consistency is disciplined reuse of verbal, visual, and experiential cues so recognition and meaning compound.",
      "Brand voice is the stable tonal and linguistic personality—formal, witty, expert, caring—applied across scripts, captions, and CTAs.",
      "Brand story is the strategic narrative of why the brand exists, whom it serves, and what change it stands for—guiding campaigns without replacing tactical storytelling craft.",
      "Brand guidelines specify approved usage of logo, color, type, imagery, voice, and motion so teams execute consistently.",
      "Logo usage rules define how the mark may appear—sizing, clear space, backgrounds, and forbidden treatments—across video frames and end cards.",
      "Visual identity is the coordinated graphic system that makes brand materials instantly recognizable and emotionally on-tone."
    ],
